{"book":9,"chapter":22,"context":{"chapter":22,"title":"The Massacre at Nob","summary":"David gathers four hundred desperate men at the cave of Adullam and places his parents under the protection of the king of Moab. Doeg tells Saul that the priests helped David; Saul's guards refuse to kill them, so Doeg slaughters eighty-five priests. Only Abiathar escapes to David.","background":"Adullam lay in Judah's western foothills. David's great-grandmother Ruth was a Moabite, which may explain why he sought refuge for his parents in Moab. The massacre partly fulfills the word against Eli's house (2:31-33), and the title of Psalm 52 links that psalm to Doeg's betrayal.","customs":[{"term":"Linen ephod","verses":"22:18","note":"The simple linen garment worn by priests while serving; the slain men were plainly priests."}],"watchFor":["Saul appeals to his tribe's self-interest (vv. 7–8).","Saul's own men refuse; a foreigner carries out the order (vv. 17–18).","David accepts responsibility: 'I have occasioned the death' (v. 22)."],"connections":["1 Samuel 2:31-33","Ruth 4:17","Psalms 52:1","Psalms 142:1"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֵּלֶךְ","vaiyelekh","H1980","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he went"],["דָּוִד","david","H1732","HNpm","David"],["מִשָּׁם","misham","H8033","HR/D","from there"],["וַיִּמָּלֵט","vaiyimalet","H4422","Hc/VNw3ms","and he escaped"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["מְעָרַת","me'arat","H4631","HNcfsc","[the] cave of"],["עֲדֻלָּם","'adulam","H5725","HNpl","Adullam"],["וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ","vaiyishme'u","H8085","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they heard"],["אֶחָיו","'echav","H251","HNcmpc/Sp3ms","brothers his"],["וְכָל","vekhol","H3605","HC/Ncmsc","and all"],["בֵּית","beit","H1004","HNcmsc","[the] household of"],["אָבִיו","'aviv","H1","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","father his"],["וַיֵּרְדוּ","vaiyeredu","H3381","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they went down"],["אֵלָיו","'elav","H413","HRd/Sp3ms","to him"],["שָׁמָּה","shamah","H8033","HD/Sd","there towards"]],"x":[[19057001,19057011,5],[13011015,13011015,4],[19034001,1903400